  "surface": "backend",
  "riskClass": "high",
  "title": "supplier-service auth has no refresh token mechanism — 24-hour access tokens cannot be revoked until expiry",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: auth_rbac. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The supplier-service auth issues a single JWT access token with 24-hour expiry (line 104: `expiresIn: '24h'`) but provides NO refresh token mechanism and NO token revocation capability. The main auth-service implements: (1) short-lived access tokens + long-lived refresh tokens, (2) refresh token rotation, (3) idle timeout, (4) session management (list/revoke), (5) Redis blacklist for immediate revocation. Supplier tokens have NONE of these. If a supplier account is compromised, the attacker has 24 hours of irrevocable access. The `generateSupplierToken` function (line 91-107) also doesn't set a `jti` claim, making it impossible to add blacklisting later without code changes.",
  "status": "done",
  "severity": "P1",
